nodes.body:
@orozery reduced the PR to the manager-level pinning fix. `lookup()` now protects reported primary HITs until `prepare_load()` / `create_store_job()` takes ownership, with release at schedule end, request finish, and reset. The batch probe/promote, P2P, and KVCR changes are decoupled.

The deterministic failing case is capacity 1: `lookup(A)=HIT`, then `lookup(B)` promotes from a secondary tier and evicts A before the scheduler consumes it. The new regression tests cover that path plus transfer and cleanup handoff.

Final head `50eaee6a4d`: 700 passed, 1 skipped (optional `kvcr` package unavailable); pre-commit passed.

